          <caption>
            <p>Membranoproliferative Pattern of Injury: PSA and Trichrome Stains. The image illustrates a membranoproliferative pattern of injury with some peripheral capillary loops containing intracapillary material referred to as pseudothrombi. (A) Glomerular basement membrane multilayering (arrow) and intracapillary pseudothrombi (arrowhead) (PAS, 600&#x000d7;). (B) Intracapillary pseudothrombi material (arrowhead) (Trichrome, 600&#x000d7;). PAS: periodic acid-Schiff. Contributed by&#x000a0;C Dernell, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Unknown" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
