        <fig id="article-169703.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Immunofluorescence in Mixed Cryoglobulinemic Glomerulonephritis. The image shows segmental capillary wall and subtle mesangial staining for IgM (A), IgG (B), C3 (C), and kappa (D) and lambda (E) light chains. IgM: Immunoglobulin M, IgG: Immunoglobulin G. Contributed by C Dernell, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Unknown-1" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
